  CONTRAST  beta_pinned - beta_unpinned = +0.1018  (SE 0.0761, z = +1.34, p = 0.181)
            95% CI [-0.0475, +0.2510]

  A pinned dependency and an unpinned one carry indistinguishable install
  risk on this corpus. What predicts failure is HOW MANY dependencies you
  declare, not whether you fixed their versions.

  This is a BOUNDED null, not a bare p > 0.05. See the power curve at the
  bottom: a true contrast of 0.30 is detected 95%% of the time at this n and
  0.20 is detected 75%% of the time, on the corpus's own covariates. The 95%%
  interval excludes
  any extra per-e-fold odds multiplier for pinning above 1.29, and any
  protective multiplier below 0.95. A pinning effect large enough to
  matter to anybody would have been visible at this n.

  For scale, the effect that IS there: exp(beta_pinned) = 1.44 per e-fold of
  pinned dependencies. Going from 5 declared dependencies to 50 multiplies
  the odds of total install failure by about 2.2.

SENSITIVITY -- the outcome could reasonably be defined two ways
  ALL executions hit install error (used above)  events=420  pinned +0.364  unpinned +0.262  contrast +0.102 (p=0.181)
  ANY execution hit install error                events=499  pinned +0.390  unpinned +0.387  contrast +0.003 (p=0.971)

